---
const brand = "HireReady";
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Sample ATS Resume Report | {brand}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="See what an ATS resume analysis report looks like before you buy." />
    <style>
      body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; max-width: 760px; margin: 30px auto; padding: 0 20px; line-height: 1.6; color: #1f2937; }
      a { color: #2563eb; }
      .note { background: #fef3c7; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; }
      .score { font-size: 40px; font-weight: bold; color: #d97706; }
      table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
      th, td { border: 1px solid #d1d5db; padding: 8px 12px; text-align: left; }
      .bad { color: #b91c1c; } .ok { color: #047857; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <p><a href="/">&larr; {brand}</a></p>
    <h1>Sample ATS Resume Report</h1>
    <p class="note"><b>Sample only.</b> This is an example with made-up data to show the format. Your report will be based on your own resume.</p>

    <h2>Overall result</h2>
    <p class="score">68 / 100</p>
    <p>Good content, but some formatting and keyword problems may stop software from reading it properly.</p>

    <h2>Formatting review</h2>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Check</th><th>Result</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Single-column layout</td><td class="ok">Pass</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Standard section headings</td><td class="ok">Pass</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Tables or text boxes</td><td class="bad">Found in Skills section</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Contact details in header</td><td class="bad">May be missed. Move to the main body</td></tr>
    </table>

    <h2>Keyword analysis (for a Python Developer job post)</h2>
    <p><b class="ok">Found:</b> Python, SQL, Git, OOP</p>
    <p><b class="bad">Missing:</b> REST API, Flask, unit testing, Linux</p>
    <p>Add a missing keyword only if it truly describes your experience.</p>

    <h2>Suggestions</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Replace the Skills table with a simple comma-separated list.</li>
      <li>Add a result to your project bullets, for example how many users or records it handled.</li>
      <li>Add a GitHub link next to your LinkedIn link.</li>
    </ol>

    <p><a href="/#resume-analysis">Get your own analysis</a> | <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a></p>
  </body>
</html>